<title>BRAZIL: Brazil govt to profit from new corp law - paper.</title>
<headline>Brazil govt to profit from new corp law - paper.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's government and majority shareholders of publicly traded firms stand to profit most from a new corporate law approved last week by the Senate, local financial daily Gazeta Mercantil said.</p>
<p>Gazeta, citing experts in Brazilian economic law, said the legislation will make it easier for the government to complete ongoing privatizations in the electrical and telecommunications sector.</p>
<p>It also benefits holding companies and majority shareholders of firms by eliminating some minority shareholder rights, the paper said.</p>
<p>(--James Craig, Sao Paulo newsroom 5511 2485413)</p>
